\newlabel{tab:factorial-contrasts}{{4}{9}{Key strict block-complete factorial contrasts in percentage points, shown as seed-level mean [95\% Student-$t$ interval]. Positive $\Delta $Worst is better, whereas positive $\Delta $Gap is worse; positive LongBench $\Delta $F1 is better. These contrasts predate the realized-subset correction; complete per-seed contrasts, within-seed paired bootstrap intervals, and Holm-adjusted tests are included in the released analysis files}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Representative-seed short-context regression checks. MMLU is full-test format-robust option accuracy and IFEval is official strict prompt accuracy. Noninferiority passes only when the paired 95\% interval for treatment minus Base lies entirely above the frozen $-2$ pp margin. JSON validity is audited separately and is not required for MMLU correctness.}}{9}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
